Repository: a project folder whose full change history is tracked.
Commit: a saved snapshot of your changes, with a message.
Branch: a separate line of development, so you can work without affecting the main code.
Merge: combining one branch’s changes into another.
Version control: a system that records changes over time so you can review, compare, and revert them, and so several people can collaborate.
Pull request: a request to merge your branch into another, usually reviewed first
